# What never belongs in the build context.
#
# The first two lines are the ones that matter. .git is most of the repository's bytes and none of its
# build inputs, and node_modules is platform-specific — a context that carried one built on a laptop
# would produce an image whose front end was linked against the wrong architecture's esbuild.
.git
.github
**/node_modules

# Build output. Every one of these is produced inside the image by the stage that needs it, and a stale
# local copy in the context is a way to ship yesterday's UI.
/dist
/public
/web/dist
/web/.angular
/internal/server/assets/*
!/internal/server/assets/.gitignore
!/internal/server/assets/PLACEHOLDER.md

# Nothing here is a build input, and the last two are the reason this file has a `*.key` line at all: a
# context is copied into the daemon whole, and a signing key that reached a build layer would be in
# every image published from it.
/testfleet
/docs
coverage.txt
*.test
*.pem
*.key
/deploy/.env
.DS_Store
.idea
.vscode
